Third-party material in benchmarks/
===================================

tpu_verilog, tpu_spire
----------------------

Derived from LogikBench, https://github.com/zeroasiccorp/logikbench,
commit e8c7c4388c66302c6adb235678512ce62b79968a (e8c7c43), directory
logikbench/benchmarks/large/tpu/rtl/.

  Copyright (c) 2025 Zero ASIC Corporation
  Author (per the source file headers): Andreas Olofsson
  License: MIT. The upstream LICENSE file of that commit is reproduced
  verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  tpu_verilog/_debug/orig/tpu.v, tpu_array.v, tpu_pe.v
      Verbatim copies of the upstream RTL.
  tpu_verilog/context/starting_point.v
      tpu_pe.v + tpu_array.v + tpu.v concatenated, otherwise unmodified.
  tpu_spire/context/starting_point.py
      A Spire HDL port of the same design (register-for-register mirror),
      written for this suite.
  tpu_*/vectors.dat
      Stimulus generated by tpu_verilog/_debug/gen_stimuli.py, with the
      expected outputs recorded from the upstream RTL through
      tpu_verilog/_debug/tb_golden_dump.sv.

The testbench (tb.sv), the stimulus generator, the task descriptions and the
metadata files were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at
the root of this repository.

jpeg_idct_2d_verilog
--------------------

Derived from core_jpeg, https://github.com/ultraembedded/core_jpeg (main
branch, 2026-07), files src_v/jpeg_idct_x.v, jpeg_idct_transpose.v,
jpeg_idct_transpose_ram.v, jpeg_idct_y.v.

  Copyright 2020 Ultra-Embedded.com (per the source file headers)
  License: Apache License 2.0. The upstream LICENSE file is reproduced
  verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE-core_jpeg.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  jpeg_idct_2d_verilog/context/starting_point.v
      The four upstream modules, unmodified, under a thin top module
      (jpeg_idct_2d) that composes them exactly as the original jpeg_idct.v
      instantiates them (downstream ready tied high).
  jpeg_idct_2d_verilog/vectors.dat
      Stimulus generated by _debug/gen_vectors.py, with the expected outputs
      recorded from the upstream RTL (recipe in _debug/README.md).

The testbench (tb.sv), the stimulus generator, the task description and the
metadata file were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at
the root of this repository.
